get ready to dive into the battlefield  in for honor master the medieval  weaponry as the bold Knights brutal  Vikings and lethal samurai prepare for  vicious fast-paced melee combat and  become the ultimate warrior but which of  the three legendary factions will you  choose here's what you need to know to  win glory as the Knights brought to you  by for honor the Knights of ash felled  were sent by the iron legions to pacify  the land they believed that the ancient  ruins that cover their lands were built  by their ancestors of the great Empire  scattered for centuries they have now  corralled under a single banner by  Asheville's black stone legion in  joining the Knights of the iron Legion  you select from heroes that are powerful  highly skilled and deadly you get the  chance to wield massive swords flails or  a sword and dagger combination Master  the Knights in order to take down the  Vikings and Samurai here's what we know  about Knights subclasses so far the  wardens are jack of all trade Knights  that are easy to use for beginners they  strike a balance between defense and  offense and feature a wide range of  basic abilities wardens wear partial  plate armor with chainmail and leather  and wield massive two-handed long swords  wardens are best with light quick  attacks especially against light heroes  their heavy swings pack a punch however  the time it takes to swing leaves them  wide open and easy to counter-attack  warden light attacks are too quick to  block if done right and our best by  doing dueling down your opponent's  health for one heavy finishing strike  combining one heavy attack followed by a  string of light quick attacks will keep  your opponent on their toes and under  your control with Swift sword attacks  and heavy armor to protect you enemies  such as the samurai won't stand a chance  conquerors are defensive fighters  recommended for playing at medium  difficulty they are heavily armored and  armed with massive flails they  destabilize opponents through multiple  defensive abilities the conqueror is an  excellent blocker with high attack  strength and heavy damage to back it up  thanks to their large shield conquerors  can block a little faster than other  heroes the downside to being a great  defensive character is that conquerors  lengthy wind-ups make it easy for more  nimble classes to dodge but if timed  right a block followed by a stun attack  will allow any conqueror to move in with  a few heavy swings before an opponent  can recover the Vikings Raider will fall  to their knees to the combined might of  your shield and skull shattering flail  the mid-level peacekeepers are fast and  lethal they use a combination of a sword  and dagger to inflict lead damage they  have limited range but high mobility  peacekeepers are hit-and-run masters on  the battlefield able to take capture  points more quickly and harass enemies  with quick cuts and fast dodging be  aware that peacekeepers have low armor  and just a few heavy hits will finish  one off light attacks followed by your  stun ability will keep an opponent off  their game allowing you to dodge attacks  with ease and finish them off with a  heavy strike soon we will learn about  the newest subclass of the Nights the  law bringers pledged your sword to the  Knights of the iron Legion and join the  war of the factions be sure to check out  our other videos to learn about the  other factions samurai and Vikings  brought to you by for honor for honor is  available on February 14th 2017 and for  all your for honor needs stick with  GameSpot
 

